methodology-audit-recon.md
# docs/ holds two kinds of markdown: real project documentation that IS committed,
# and generated analysis output (recon reports, audits, per-step summaries) that is
# NOT. This is an ALLOWLIST, deliberately: ignore every .md in docs/, then re-admit
# the real docs by exact name below.
#
# Why this direction: the previous denylist (docs/*-recon.md, docs/*-audit.md,
# docs/step-*.md, ...) made the NAMING CONVENTION load-bearing — a new analysis file
# that didn't happen to match a pattern (docs/cvq-notes.md) got committed silently.
# Failing that way is the bad one, and that reasoning still holds.
#
# WHAT THIS COMMENT USED TO CLAIM, AND WHY IT WAS WRONG. It said the worst case was
# "a real doc staying untracked until someone adds a `!` line, which `git status`
# makes obvious". git status does NOT make it obvious: it never lists an ignored
# file, which is the entire point of ignoring one. `git status --ignored` does, and
# nobody runs it.
#
# The cost of that mistake, measured 2026-09-08: SIXTEEN docs/*.md files cited from
# code do not exist and never did — `git log --all` shows zero commits touching any
# of them. Among them are docs/v2-rebuild-plan.md and docs/v2-phase3-recon.md, which
# shared/assessmentFlow.ts:4-11 cites as its SPEC and as the reason the module
# exists. Sixteen documents went missing without anyone noticing, exactly as this
# comment said would be survivable.
#
# So: the allowlist direction is right, and the safety net named here is imaginary.
# If you write a doc under docs/ that anything else will cite, add its `!` line IN
# THE SAME COMMIT as the citation. Nothing will remind you later.
#
# ADDING A REAL PROJECT DOC? Add a matching `!docs/<name>.md` line here, or it will
# not be tracked. Analysis output needs no entry — it is ignored by default.
#
# Only *.md is ignored, so the .docx/.html white papers in docs/ are unaffected.
docs/*.md
!docs/DATABASE_INDEXES_MIGRATION.md
!docs/PAID_REPORT_ENHANCEMENT_SPEC.md
!docs/REPORT_TIER_COMPARISON.md
!docs/VALUES_PROFILE_DERIVATION_METHODOLOGY.md
!docs/career-sourcing-map.md
!docs/uae-official-sectors.md
!docs/v2-phase4-recon.md
!docs/v2-phase4-step4-recon.md
!docs/v2-phase5-recon.md
